  "note": "Verso page carrying TWO stacked worked-example panels and no running prose, so one `full` column over the live area 0.128-0.904 is declared. Panel 1 [0.3141, 0.1345, 0.8871, 0.4669] finishes Example 1.8 (blocks n=1..n=4); panel 2 [0.3141, 0.4734, 0.8871, 0.9371] is Example 1.9 (blocks n=5..n=11 plus Fig. 1.14) and runs off the foot. Both sample #dbdcde in their flat interior. Each panel has its own wide white-on-cyan label bar - 'EXAMPLE 1.8' and 'EXAMPLE 1.9' - on the OUTER (left) edge at x 0.262-0.304 (major_heading, so that role appears twice here), and a thin plain cyan #00adef bar on the inner (right) edge (decorative_image, likewise twice). Block n=3 is three stacked decks of one derivation (a_p = eE/m_p, the substituted fraction, and the result) taken by A2 as a single equation, hence its 0.10-tall bbox. The 'FIGURE 1.14' caption has no A2 block and carries n: null; it is cyan #00adef on the panel grey. No footer_rule. Folio '22' in a pale cyan box in the outer bottom margin; '2022-23' recorded as running_header."
